      "message": "ISTM the heaviest operation in this test is the registering of the requests. A good part of that processing time is likely spent doing the rematch.\n\nHistorically the rematch was network-major, so we\u0027d have to rematch everything whenever a new request is filed. The code still dates from that period, and handleRegisterNetworkRequests calls rematchAllNetworksAndRequests(). That means we try to match Σ(n \u003d 1 → 250, n) \u003d 30k+ requests.\n\nNow the rematch is request-major, and it\u0027s easy to rematch only one request, for a lightening of the load of a factor of 250.\n\nIf we replace rematchAllNetworksAndRequests() with rematchNetworksAndRequests(nris), does that (pass the tests and) provide the speed boost necessary to keep this under the current timeout ? It would also be good for resource consumption.",
